---
description: When handing over verified work, state what was checked, the evidence, and spot-checks.
alwaysApply: true
---

When delivering verified work, follow `verify-handoff`:

1. What you verified — the checks you actually ran (not "looks good").
2. The evidence — commands run, outputs seen, URLs checked.
3. Suggested spot-checks — 1–3 specific things worth a human glance.

Never report work as done without testing it first. If you cannot test, say so explicitly instead of implying it.

Read `~/.cursor/skills/verify-handoff/SKILL.md` (or `.cursor/skills/verify-handoff/SKILL.md`).
